  <object class="pygubu.builder.widgets.dialog" id="helpDialog">
    <property name="height">600</property>
    <property name="maxsize">600|600</property>
    <property name="minsize">600|600</property>
    <property name="resizable">none</property>
    <property name="title" translatable="yes">MDMT - OCR Documentation</property>
    <property name="width">600</property>
    <child>
      <object class="pygubu.builder.widgets.tkinterscrolledtext" id="helpText">
        <property name="padx">10</property>
        <property name="pady">10</property>
        <property name="state">disabled</property>
        <property name="text" translatable="yes">Program Documentation
=========================================================
GENERAL
=========================================================
The OCR tool extracts text from image-based PDF files, making the content searchable and selectable. It uses Tesseract OCR under the hood.

Note: OCR won't work with password-protected PDFs and will invalidate digitally signed PDFs.

Note: Unless "Redo Existing OCR" is enabled, files that are already text-selectable will be skipped.
=========================================================
INPUT
=========================================================
Select PDF Directory:

Click the ellipsis icon to select a directory containing your PDFs. All PDF files in this directory and its subdirectories will be processed. The original directory structure will be recreated in the output directory.
=========================================================
OUTPUT
=========================================================
Select Output Directory:

Click the ellipsis icon to select where OCR'd PDFs will be saved. This cannot be the same as the input directory.
=========================================================
LANGUAGES
=========================================================
Select the language(s) your PDFs contain from the list. When a "(Script)" option is available, it will automatically select all languages using that script. For example, "Ethiopic (Script)" selects both Amharic and Tigrinya.
=========================================================
OPTIONS
=========================================================
PDF/A Output (Archive Ready):
Creates archive-ready PDFs in the output directory. Enable only if needed.

Extract Text to Text File:
Creates a plain text file alongside each OCR'd PDF, containing just the extracted text. Useful for text analysis projects.

Redo Existing OCR:
Discards any existing OCR and re-OCRs using Tesseract. If disabled, already OCR'd PDFs in the input will be skipped.

Correct Page Rotation:
Auto-rotates pages to an upright orientation based on the selected confidence threshold.

Confidence Threshold:
Determines how certain the tool must be that a page needs rotation before rotating it. Low confidence risks false positives, high risks false negatives. Choose based on your PDF quality.

Correct Skewed Scans:
Auto-straightens page text. Works best on significantly skewed text (>4 degrees).
